```text
PUBLIC SERVICES COMMITTEE
MINUTES
A meeting of the Public Services Committee was held on Monday, August 18, 2025. in Council
Chambers and via electronic meeting, starting at 12:00 p.m. Those in attendance were as follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS:
Tom Segrave, Chairman: Dr. Michelle Aldrich; Dr. Kathy
Emmons; and Jeff White.
AGENDA ITEMS
12.
ORDINANCE —2 READING
— Annexing to the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, land
northeast of the intersection of Frontier Mall Drive and Rue Terre Avenue and west of
Converse Avenue (SPONSOR
— MR. SEGRAVE)
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 2 reading, seconded by Mr. White.
Motion carried by
unanimous voice vote.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department Senior Planner, provided a staff report.
13.
ORDINANCE 2’ READING
— Amending the Official Zoning Map of the City of
Cheyenne, establishing the zoning classification of CB
— Community Business for land
annexed to the City of Cheyenne located northeast of the intersection of Frontier Mall
Drive and Rue Terre Avenue and west of Converse Avenue. (SPONSOR
— MR.
SEGRAVE)
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 2 reading, seconded by Dr. Emmons.
Motion carried by
unanimous voice vote.
Connor White. Planning & Development Department Senior Planner, provided a staff report.
14.
ORDINANCE —2” READING
— Amending the Official Zoning Map of the City of
Cheyenne, changing the zoning classification for land located southwest of the intersection
of llolland Court and Ridge Road from AG
— Agricultural to NR-2- Neighborhood
Residential
— Medium Density. (SPONSOR
- MR. SEGRAVE)
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 2d reading. seconded by Mr. White.
Motion carried by
unanimous voice vote.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department Senior Planner. provided a staff report and
advised the property previously was considered for a zone change to NR-3
— Neighborhood
Residential
- high Density’, and failed the approval process. Brad Emmons, AVI P.C.. and Jason
Stevens. Bedrock Development LLC,
provided additional information related to the proposed
zoning.
Committee members Aldrich and Emmons commented on the item.
Public comments
were made by Elizabeth Gillispie, Amber Luthi, and Rebecca Murchie.
```

### Page 2 of 2

```text
15.
ORDINANCE _2m1 READING
— Creating Section 10.24.200, Vehicle Mufflers, Excessive
Smoke and Unreasonable Noise, and repealing Section 8.56.050, Motor Vehicle Mufflers,
of the Municipal Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, to revise and enhance
provisions governing vehicle mufflers and noise, to establish a graduated penalty structure
for recurring offenses, and to make conforming amendments as specified. (SPONSORS
—
DR. ALDRICH. MR. MOODY & MR. SEGRAVE)
Mr. White moved to approve on
reading. seconded by Dr. Aldrich. Dr. Aldrich moved to
postpone until the September 8,2025, governing body meeting, seconded by Dr. Emmons. Motion
to postpone carried by unanimous voice vote.
Chairman Segrave made an announcement to those present that the proposed ordinance change
would likely be postponed for additional editing.
John Brodie, City Attorney, provided a staff
report and Captain David Janes, Police Department. provided additional infornmtion related to the
enforcement of the current and proposed ordinance, All committee members commented on the
item, as did Ward I Councilman Pete Labyourn.
Public comments were made by Ryan Blue,
Dameon Degreenia, Ron Dickerson, Jessi Eblen. Paul Fanning, and Suzanne Robins.
There being no further items for the agenda to come before the Public Services Committee, the
meeting was adjourned at 12:59 p.m.
Submitted by,
9.yntt&at
Jennifer MeClelland
Executive Assistant to the Cheyenne City Council
